# KubeOS: questions for the guided disk layout (Proxmox-VE style).
#
# WHEN   Loaded by main-menu at installer start-up
#        (usr/lib/main-menu.d/94-kubeos-layout), before any screen is drawn.
# WHY    The installer asks five things and builds everything else itself: the
#        1 MiB bios_grub area, the EFI partition, the LVM volume group and the
#        root/swap logical volumes. cdebconf silently drops a question that was
#        never loaded, so these must be registered before partman starts.
#        Where the layout comes from: usr/lib/partman/init.d/06-kubeos-layout.
# SAFE   Data only: no code runs from this file.
#
# Wording rule (user decision, 2026-11-09): swap and root get a bare label with
# no explanation; only minfree and maxdata carry a one-line meaning. Do not add
# explanatory paragraphs back to the others.
#
# Choices of kubeos/layout-disk are supplied at run time with db_subst DISKS
# (the same ${VARIABLE} mechanism grub-installer uses for its device list).
# A comma separates choices, so the script strips commas from disk models.

Template: kubeos/layout-disk
Type: select
Choices: ${DISKS}
Description: Disk:

Template: kubeos/layout-disk-info
Type: note
Description: ${DISK}: ${SIZE} total, ${USABLE} usable.

Template: kubeos/layout-swap
Type: string
Description: Swap size (GiB):

Template: kubeos/layout-root
Type: string
Description: Root size (GiB):

Template: kubeos/layout-minfree
Type: string
Description: Minfree (GiB), minimum amount of hdsize that must remain unused:

Template: kubeos/layout-maxdata
Type: string
Description: Maxdata (GiB), size of the data partition for pods and containers:

Template: kubeos/layout-bad-number
Type: error
Description: Enter a whole number of GiB.

Template: kubeos/layout-root-small
Type: error
Description: Root must be at least ${MIN} GiB.

Template: kubeos/layout-does-not-fit
Type: critical
Description: Does not fit on ${DISK}.
 swap ${SWAP} + root ${ROOT} + minfree ${MINFREE} + maxdata ${MAXDATA} (GiB) exceeds the ${USABLE} GiB usable on this disk.

Template: kubeos/layout-data-small
Type: critical
Description: Not enough left for maxdata: ${LEFT} GiB available, ${MIN} GiB minimum.

Template: kubeos/layout-no-disk
Type: critical
Description: No fixed disk found.

# Shown only when partman refuses an answer this installer wrote itself. It
# exists so a silent fall-back to partman's own guided menu is impossible: the
# user gets the exact question and the value partman actually stored, which is
# what a bug report needs. See init.d/06-kubeos-layout, section 6.
Template: kubeos/layout-not-accepted
Type: critical
Description: The installer could not hand its layout to partman.
 ${QUESTION} was set to "${WANTED}" but partman has "${GOT}".
 The disk will not be partitioned automatically.
